### Instruction:
Write code to delete an element of a linked list given its position.

### Input:
Linked List: 8->3->65->7
Position: 2

### Response:
public class LinkedList {

    Node head;

    static class Node {
        int data;
        Node next;

        Node(int d) {
            data = d;
            next = null;
        }
    }

    public void deleteNode(int position) {
        if (head == null) {
            return;
        }
        Node temp = head;

        if(position == 0){
            head = temp.next;
            return;
        }

        for (int i = 0; temp != null && i < position - 1; i++) {
            temp = temp.next;
        }

        if (temp == null || temp.next == null) {
            return;
        }

        // Unlink the deleted node from the linked list
        Node next = temp.next.next;
        temp.next = next; 
    }

}

### Instruction:
Design a stack using a dynamic array in Java.

### Response:
class MyStack { 
    int top; 
    int capacity; 
    int stack[]; 

    // Creating stack 
    MyStack(int capacity) 
    { 
        this.capacity = capacity; 
        stack = new int[capacity]; 
        top = -1; 
    } 

    // Adding an element on top of the stack  
    public void push(int item) 
    { 
        if (top == capacity - 1){ 
            System.out.println("Stack overflow"); 
        } 
        else{ 
            stack[++top] = item; 
            System.out.println(item + " pushed into stack"); 
        } 
    } 

    // Removing an element from the stack 
    public int pop() 
    { 
        if (top == -1) { 
            System.out.println("Stack underflow"); 
            return 0; 
        } 
        else { 
            int item = stack[top--]; 
            return item; 
        } 
    } 
}

